[ti:Week02-Wed.mp3]

[00:00.00]cope 熟义 v. 对付，处理 示例 ① Christine Holm believes paternity leave provides a new kind of training for men in that it can help them cope with stress. 克里斯蒂娜•霍尔姆认为陪产假为男士们提供了一种新型的培训，因为这样可以帮助他们应对压力。（2007. 12） ② Do not imagine that you can cope with all the difficulties. 别以为你能应对所有这些困难。
[00:07.08]immerse 熟义 vt. 浸没，把…浸入；使沉浸于，使专心于 示例 ① Martin Jol likes to immerse himself in his ever-expanding art collection. 马丁•约尔喜欢沉浸在自己不断扩大的艺术收藏中。（The Times）② After graduation, I immersed myself in my career. 毕业以后，我全身心投入我的事业当中。
[00:12.79]shrink 熟义 v. （使）缩水；收缩；畏缩‖n. 收缩； 畏缩 示例 ① But over the next few decades labour forces in rich countries are set to shrink so much that inflows of immigrants would have to increase enormously to compensate: to at least twice their current size in western Europe's most youthful countries, and three times in the older ones. 但是在接下来的几十年中，富裕国家的劳动力数量势必会大幅度缩减，要填补这一缺口需要大量的移民流入：在西欧， 一些最年轻的国家所需移民数量至少为目前的两倍，而在一些老龄化比较严重的国家， 所需移民数量为目前的三倍。 （2010. 12） ② The little boy shrank away from me when I tried to talk to him. 当我试图和这个小男孩说话时，他避开了我。
[00:26.34]manufacture 熟义 v. 制造；加工；捏造‖n. 制造；[pl.] 工业品；制造业 示例 ① Facing fierce competition from other companies, the automobile manufacturer is considering launching a promotion campaign. 面对来自其他公司的激烈竞争，汽车制造商正在考虑开展促销活动。（2012. 6） ② This firm manufactures buses. 这家公司生产公共汽车。
[00:33.23]claim 熟义 v. 声称；要求；索要‖n. 声明；所有权；索赔 示例 ① Although Wright Vigar hasn't yet quantified the business benefits, it claims that, in addition to being able to retain key staff with young families, it is able to save fee-earners a substantial amount of "dead" time in their working days. 尽管赖特•瓦伊格公司目前还没有评估这样做能带来多大的商业效益，但该公司称，这样做除了可以留住那些刚组建家庭不久的核心员工外，还可以减少员工工作日中的大量“窝工” 时间。（2009. 12）② His brother claimed to be the rightful heir. 他弟弟声称自己是合法继承人。
[00:44.60]weaken 熟义 v. 削弱；（使）变弱 示例 ① Stress can weaken the immune system transiently but significantly. 压力对免疫系统的削弱是短暂的，却又是显著的。（New Scientist）② Malnutrition weakens the patient. 营养不良导致病人身体虚弱。
[00:49.41]vary 熟义 v. 改变，变化；不同；使偏离 示例 ① In the case of Facebook, the company says data may hang around until the URL in question is reused, which is usually "after a short period of time", though obviously that time can vary considerably. 至于脸谱公司，他们的说法是：那些数据可能会一直存在，直到之前提到的网址被再次使用——通常这“只需要很短的一段时间”。然而，很显然，这段时间在长短上可能会有很大差别。（2010. 12）② The prices of some goods vary with the season. 某些货物的价格随着季节的变化而变动。
[00:59.54]convince 熟义 vt. 使确信，使信服；说服 示例 ① Knight convinced the company's officials of the potential for its product in the U.S. 奈特说服了这家公司的官员，使他们相信他们公司的产品在美国也有发展潜力。 （2008. 12） ② How can I convince her of its truth? 我怎样才能说服她相信这是真的呢？
[01:05.23]severe 熟义 a. 严厉的；严重的；剧烈的 示例 ① However, plowing is blamed for causing severe damage to topsoil by removing the plants that protect soil from being blown or washed away. 然而，耕作因移除了保护土壤使其免于被风吹走或者被水冲走的植被而受到责备。（2006. 12）② You are too severe on (upon) the boy. 你对那个男孩太严厉了。
[01:12.06]reconcile 熟义 vt. 使和解；使协调；使顺从（甘心）于 示例 ① Physicists have long tried to reconcile them in a theory of quantum gravity—with only limited success. 物理学家长久以来一直尝试用量子引力理论使它们协调一致，但是收效甚微。（Scientific American） ② She felt a little more reconciled to her lot. 她感到对自己的命运多少接受一些了。
[01:18.99]subsidiary 熟义 n. 子公司；附属机构‖a. 辅助的；补贴的；附属的 示例 ① In January 2008 the site released stolen documents from Julius Baer, a Swiss bank, including bank records of about 1,600 clients with accounts at a subsidiary in the Cayman Islands. 2008年1 月，该网站披露了瑞士（私人）银行宝盛集团（Julius Baer）的一份失窃文件，内容包括其在开曼群岛一家子公司约1,600名客户的银行记录。（The Economist） ② I plan to study chemistry as a subsidiary course. 我打算辅修化学。
[01:29.00]facilitate 熟义 vt. 促进；使容易；帮助 示例 ① Internet-based telecoms facilitates remote working by offering sophisticated voice services. 基于互联网的电信通过提供成熟的语音服务为远程办公提供支持。（2009. 12） ② The new road will facilitate the development of tourism. 新路将促进旅游业的发展。
[01:35.32]symptom 熟义 n. 症状；征兆 示例 ① Fatigue is a typical symptom of lack of exercise. 疲劳是缺乏锻炼的典型症兆。 （2010. 6）② The doctor made his diagnosis after studying the patient's symptoms. 医生研究病人的症状后，做出了诊断。
[01:40.09]fashion 熟义 n. 时尚；风格；方式，方法‖vt. 形成； 塑造 示例 ① One might well imagine little girls using exceedingly polite forms when playing house or imitating older women— in a fashion analogous to little girls' use of a high-pitched voice to do "teacher talk" or "mother talk" in role play. 人们可以想像出一个小女孩使用极度礼貌的形式玩过家家或者模仿年长的女性——以一种类似于角色扮演中小女孩使用高声调模仿老师或者母亲的言谈的方式。（2007. 6）② Research shows that men are beginning to follow fashion. 研究显示，男性也开始追求时尚。
[01:51.25]vulnerable 熟义 a. 易受伤害的；有弱点的；脆弱的 示例 ① Are cities and towns less safe and kids more vulnerable to crimes like child kidnap and sexual abuse than they were in previous generations? 是城镇变得更危险，还是比起前几代人，现在的孩子们更容易受到儿童绑架和性虐待等犯罪的伤害呢？（2009. 6）② The potato is vulnerable to several pests. 马铃薯易受几种害虫的侵害。
[01:58.84]scare 熟义 n. 惊吓，惊恐‖v. 受惊吓；恐吓 示例 ① There is nothing like the suggestion of a cancer risk to scare a parent, especially one of the over-educated, eco-conscious type. 没有什么事情会比孩子有患上癌症的风险更让父母感到害怕了，尤其是对那些有着超高的学历且对生态环境很敏感的父母来说。 （2009. 12） ② The high price is scaring away possible buyers. 价格昂贵，把想买东西的顾客吓跑了。
[02:06.64]analogy 熟义 n. 类似，类比，类推 示例 ① Quick to come from her lips is contempt for the analogy that human memory works like a computer hard disk, on which data are cleanly written and from which data are accurately read back. 有人将人脑的记忆类比成电脑硬盘，数据被清晰地写入，也可以被准确地读取。她很快表达了对这一类比的蔑视。（Scientific American） ② It is not always reliable to argue by analogy. 用类推法论证并不总是可靠的。
[02:15.65]aggravate 熟义 vt. 加重，使恶化；使恼火 示例 ① The increasing popularity of the scooter has aggravated the problem, providing more water vehicles to compete for the same space. 水上摩托的普及使这一问题变得更严重了，提供了更多水上交通工具来竞争同一块儿水域。（2008. 6）② Stress and lack of sleep can aggravate the situation. 压力和睡眠不足会使情况恶化。
[02:23.06]distinct 熟义 a. 明显的；截然不同的；独特的 示例 ① When a noted leader on the art of management, Peter Drucker, coined the phrase "Management is doing things right; leadership is doing the right things," he was seeking to clarify the distinctions he associates with the terms. 当管理艺术方面的一位著名领军人物彼得•德鲁克创造性地阐明“管理是把事情做好，而领导力是做正确的事情”时，他是在试图澄清他所联系起来的这两个术语之间的差异。（2011. 12） ② I had the distinct impression that I was followed. 我确实感到有人在跟踪我。
[02:33.89]correspondent 熟义 n. 通讯记者；通信者‖a. 与…一致的； 相应的 示例 ① In 1973, Claude Vorilhon, a correspondent for a French racing-car magazine, claimed to have been whisked away in a flying saucer, in which he had spent six days with a green chap who spoke fluent French. 1973年，一家法国赛车杂志的记者克劳德•佛里昂宣称他曾被一只飞碟带走，并与飞碟里一个能说流利法语的绿色家伙共度了6天时光。（The Economist） ② The result was correspondent with what I expected. 结果与我所期望的一致。
[02:44.14]occupancy 熟义 n. 占有，占领；居住 示例 ① Driving in the high-occupancy vehicle lane without a passenger carries a $478 penalty. 在没有乘客的情况下，驾车驶入高乘载率车道将被处以478美元的罚金。（The Times）② He took occupancy of this position for more than ten years. 他担任这一职位超过十年了。
[02:50.31]myth 熟义 n. 神话；奇人；虚构的人或事 ‖vt. 使神话化 示例 ① So we've contrived various justifications that turn out to be half-truths, prejudices or myths. 所以我们发明了很多自认为有理的辩护，这些辩护成了半真半假的陈词、偏见和荒诞的说法。（2008. 6） ② The story is a pure myth. 这故事纯属虚构。
[02:56.08]enable 熟义 v. 使能够，使可能，使可行 示例 ① Etzioni says the booming economy of the last decade enabled those individuals with poor motives to get rich before getting in trouble. 埃奇奥尼说，最近十年经济的高速发展让那些怀有不良动机的人在遇上麻烦之前发了财。（2006. 12）② Only teamwork will enable us to get the job done on time. 只有团队合作才能使我们按时完成这项工作。
[03:03.71]justify 熟义 vt. 证明…有理；为…辩护；对…做出解释 示例 ① As Yale law professor Anne Alstott argues, justifying parental support depends on defining the family as a social good that, in some sense, society must pay for. 耶鲁大学的法学教授安妮•阿尔斯托特认为，要想使对父母的支持合法化，就必须先把“家庭”定义为一种社会善举，且从某种意义上来说，社会需要为这种善举买单。（2010. 6）② They agreed that this decision was fully justified by economic conditions. 他们一致同意，这个决定完全符合经济情况。
[03:13.81]constituent 熟义 n. 选民；成分，构成部分‖a. 构成的； 选举的；立宪的 示例 ① Their crushing gravity fuses electrons and protons into neutrons, and at the core the neutrons may break down to their constituent quarks. 它们决定性的重力将电子和质子融合成中子，而且在核心处，中子可能分解成它们的组成成分夸克。（Scientific American） ② Punctuality is an important constituent of good character. 准时是优良品格的重要组成。
[03:22.51]modest 熟义 a. 谦虚的；适度的；端庄的 示例 ① For example, modest joggers should not compare their performance with Olympic standard marathon runners. 例如，谦虚的慢跑者不应该将他们的表现与奥林匹克标准的马拉松长跑者相比较。（2012. 12） ② She is very modest about her success. 她对自己的成就很谦虚。
[03:28.65]effective 熟义 a. 有效的；生效的；实际的 示例 ① His Seven Habits of Highly EffectivePeople became a popular bestseller very quickly. 他的著作《高效能人士的七个习惯》很快成为受欢迎的畅销书。（2011. 12）② The new rules will become effective in the next few days. 新规定将在几天后生效。
[03:34.58]parallel 熟义 n. 平行线；对比‖vt. 与…平行；相比‖a. 平行的；类似的 示例 ① Chancellor Angela Merkel drew parallels on Sunday between the risk of a Greek default now and the broader chaos in the financial system.周日，德国总理安吉拉•默克尔将希腊目前的违约风险和金融系统的广泛混乱画了等号。（The New York Times）② The trees stand in parallel with the road. 这些树与公路平行。
[03:42.35]adhere 熟义 v. 粘附 示例 ① Microsoft has also laid down minimum standards to which phone makers must adhere for things such as built-in cameras. 微软也制定了电话制造商必须遵守的诸如内置摄像头等最低标准。（The Economist） ② He always adhere to his own opinion. 他总是固执己见。
[03:48.28]breed 熟义 v. 繁殖；引起；教养‖n. 品种；血统 示例 ① To Galbraith, materialism had gone mad and would breed discontent. 对加尔布雷思而言，物质主义已经疯狂，并且会滋生不满。（2007. 6） ② If they are unemployed, it must breed resentment. 如果他们失去工作，一定会产生怨恨。
[03:53.69]extreme 熟义 a. 极端的；极限的；非常的‖n. 极端； 困境 示例 ① That's why Hallowell believes it was okay for people to indulge some extreme worries last fall by asking doctors for cipro and buying gas masks. 这就是为什么哈洛韦尔认为去年秋天人们向医生获取抗炭疽菌的药物和购买防毒面具这种陷入极度担忧的行为是可以理解的。（2006. 12） ② In old days people lived in extreme poverty. 过去人们生活极端贫困。
[04:01.74]compromise 熟义 n. 妥协；妥协(或折中)方案；折中物‖v. 折中解决；妥协，退让 示例 ① Women find it hard to combine family and career. They often compromise by having just one child. 女人发现要实现家庭与事业的完美结合很难。她们往往选择折中的办法——只要一个孩子。（2010. 12）② They found it wiser to compromise with her on that point. 他们觉得在这一点上向她妥协更明智。
[04:08.99]provision 熟义 n. 提供；[pl.] 饮食供应‖vt. 向…供应食物 示例 ① To avoid fiscal meltdown, public pensions and health-care provision will have to be reined back severely and taxes may have to go up. 为了避免财政危机，社会养老和医疗保障的供给将会被大幅削减， 税收也会提高。（2010. 12）② They ran out of provisions after a week's drifting on the sea. 在海上漂泊一周后，他们的食物吃光了。
[04:16.98]mood 熟义 n. 心情；语气；气氛 示例 ① Stress may also contribute to disease in less direct ways by influencing moods and behaviour. 压力可能通过影响情绪和行为等方式间接导致人们生病。（2008. 12）② He is a man of moods. 他是个喜怒无常的人。
[04:21.78]allege 熟义 v. 断言；宣称；提出…作为理由；指控 示例 ① But critics allege that by making electronic copies of these books without first seeking the permission of copyright holders, Google has committed piracy. 但是，批评者们称，在没有事先征得著作权人许可的前提下，谷歌将这些图书制成电子版已经构成了侵权。（2011. 12）② The newspaper reporter alleged that the man was innocent. 新闻记者宣称这个男人是无辜的。
[04:30.31]agency 熟义 n. 代理；政府机构 示例 ① The Internet had its origin in a 1969 U.S. Defense Department computer network called ARPAnet, which stand for Advanced Research Projects Agency Network. 互联网起源自1969年美国国防部建立的阿帕网，即高级研究计划署网络。（2009. 6）② My old sister was placed in Xinhua News Agency as a translator. 我姐姐被安排在新华通讯社当翻译。
[04:38.23]elite 熟义 n. 精英‖a. 杰出的，优秀的 示例 ① At the same time, perhaps inevitably, the humanities—while still popular in elite colleges and universities— have experienced a significant decline. 同时，似乎也是不可避免地，人文学科虽然在精英学院和大学还是很受欢迎的，但已经严重衰落了。（2010. 12）② Only the educational elite can go to Oxford or Cambridge University. 只有学业上的精英才能上牛津或剑桥大学。
[04:46.82]investigate 熟义 v. 调查；审查；研究 示例 ① Phil Barton, chief executive of Keep Britain Tidy, launching its new Dirty Pig campaign, said it was the first time it had investigated which brands made up "littered England" and the same names appeared again and again. “让英国保持清洁”组织发起了代号为“脏猪”的新运动，该组织的首席执行官菲尔•巴顿说这是他们第一次调查哪些品牌应该对“满是垃圾的英国”负责，以及哪些品牌的名字在调查中一次又一次地出现。（2009. 12） ② The local police are investigating the murder. 当地警方正在调查这起谋杀案。
[04:57.86]obscure 熟义 a. 鲜为人知的；费解的，难以理解的 ‖vt. 使模糊 示例 ① The old religious idiom has been replaced by a secular one, and this tends to obscure what otherwise would be obvious. 旧有的宗教习语已被世俗语言代替，这会让本来清楚的东西变得模糊。（The Economist） ② This issue has been obscured by recent events. 最近发生的一些事件使这一问题变得混淆不清。
[05:05.12]privacy 熟义 n. 隐私，秘密 示例 ① The Federal Trade Commission has come up with timely recommendations to protect privacy online. 联邦贸易委员会针对保护网络隐私提出了及时的建议。（The New York Times） ② Everyone has his own privacy. 每个人都有自己的隐私。
